NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a browser action that a page agent needs to discover and execute. WebMCP exposes your TanStack client tools through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.modelContext"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Experimental:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" WebMCP support is experimental. Use it as progressive enhancement, not as a required application path."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"During SSR, in insecure contexts, or in unsupported browsers, registration resolves without adding tools. Your application continues to work without WebMCP."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page sends your tools to WebMCP. To give the WebMCP tools on a page to your own chat, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./webmcp-page-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Page WebMCP Tools in Chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-install-the-packages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install the packages"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-react\",\"zod\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-vue\",\"zod\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-solid\",\"zod\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-svelte\",\"zod\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-preact\",\"zod\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-angular\",\"zod\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\",\"zod\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-octane\",\"octane\",\"zod\"]],\"remix\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-remix\",\"remix\",\"zod\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-define-an-executable-client-tool","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Define an executable client tool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define the tool at module scope. A browser agent executes the tool to open a help panel."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// tools.ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const openHelpPanel = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'open_help_panel',\n  description: 'Open the help panel for a topic',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    topic: z.string(),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    opened: z.boolean(),\n  }),\n}).client((input) => {\n  const panel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#help-panel')\n  if (!panel) {\n    return { opened: false }\n  }\n\n  panel.dataset.topic = input.topic\n  panel.showPopover()\n  return { opened: true }\n})\n\nexport const webMCPTools = [openHelpPanel]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebMCP requires an executable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".client()"},{"type":"text","value":" implementation. It also requires a nonempty description and a valid tool name."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool name can contain 1 to 128 ASCII letters, numbers, underscores, hyphens, or periods."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-register-the-tool","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Register the tool"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the lifecycle wrapper for your framework. Each wrapper removes its registrations during owner cleanup."}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRegisterWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" in a component. If its contents do not change, keep the tool array stable."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst webMCPOptions = {\n  onError(error: unknown) {\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\n  },\n}\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vue"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRegisterWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" in a setup scope. Vue removes the registrations during scope disposal."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nuseRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n  onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <section id=\"help-panel\" popover>\n    <h2>Help</h2>\n  </section>\n</template>","lang":"vue"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRegisterWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" in a reactive owner. Solid removes the registrations during owner cleanup."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"svelte"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRegisterWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" in the component script. Svelte removes the registrations during component destruction."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n  import { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\n  createRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n  })\n</script>\n\n<section id=\"help-panel\" popover>\n  <h2>Help</h2>\n</section>","lang":"svelte"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"preact"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRegisterWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" in a component. If its contents do not change, keep the tool array stable."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst webMCPOptions = {\n  onError(error: unknown) {\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\n  },\n}\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"angular"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectRegisterWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" in an injection context. Angular removes the registrations through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DestroyRef"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-angular'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-help-page',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: '<section id=\"help-panel\" popover><h2>Help</h2></section>',\n})\nexport class HelpPage {\n  webMCP = injectRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n  })\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"octane"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRegisterWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":" in a component. If its contents do not change, keep the tool array stable."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-octane'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst webMCPOptions = {\n  onError(error: unknown) {\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\n  },\n}\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"remix"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the component "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Handle"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRegisterWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":". Remix uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handle.signal"},{"type":"text","value":" for cleanup."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\nimport { clientEntry, createElement } from 'remix/ui'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nexport const HelpPage = clientEntry(\n  import.meta.url,\n  function HelpPage(handle) {\n    createRegisterWebMCPTools(handle, webMCPTools, {\n      onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n    })\n\n    return () =>\n      createElement(\n        'section',\n        { id: 'help-panel', popover: 'auto' },\n        createElement('h2', {}, 'Help'),\n      )\n  },\n)","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"vue\",\"solid\",\"svelte\",\"preact\",\"angular\",\"octane\",\"remix\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\\n\\nconst webMCPOptions = {\\n  onError(error: unknown) {\\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\\n  },\\n}\\n\\nexport function HelpPage() {\\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\\n\\n  return (\\n    <section id=\\\"help-panel\\\" popover=\\\"auto\\\">\\n      <h2>Help</h2>\\n    </section>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"vue\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"<script setup lang=\\\"ts\\\">\\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\\n\\nuseRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\\n  onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\\n})\\n</script>\\n\\n<template>\\n  <section id=\\\"help-panel\\\" popover>\\n    <h2>Help</h2>\\n  </section>\\n</template>\",\"language\":\"vue\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\\n\\nexport function HelpPage() {\\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\\n  })\\n\\n  return (\\n    <section id=\\\"help-panel\\\" popover=\\\"auto\\\">\\n      <h2>Help</h2>\\n    </section>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"svelte\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"<script lang=\\\"ts\\\">\\n  import { createRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\\n  import { webMCPTools } from './tools'\\n\\n  createRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\\n  })\\n</script>\\n\\n<section id=\\\"help-panel\\\" popover>\\n  <h2>Help</h2>\\n</section>\",\"language\":\"svelte\"}],\"preact\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\\n\\nconst webMCPOptions = {\\n  onError(error: unknown) {\\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\\n  },\\n}\\n\\nexport function HelpPage() {\\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\\n\\n  return (\\n    <section id=\\\"help-panel\\\" popover=\\\"auto\\\">\\n      <h2>Help</h2>\\n    </section>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"angular\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\\nimport { injectRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-angular'\\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\\n\\n@Component({\\n  selector: 'app-help-page',\\n  standalone: true,\\n  template: '<section id=\\\"help-panel\\\" popover><h2>Help</h2></section>',\\n})\\nexport class HelpPage {\\n  webMCP = injectRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\\n  })\\n}\",\"language\":\"ts\"}],\"octane\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-octane'\\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\\n\\nconst webMCPOptions = {\\n  onError(error: unknown) {\\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\\n  },\\n}\\n\\nexport function HelpPage() {\\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\\n\\n  return (\\n    <section id=\\\"help-panel\\\" popover=\\\"auto\\\">\\n      <h2>Help</h2>\\n    </section>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"remix\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\\nimport { clientEntry, createElement } from 'remix/ui'\\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\\n\\nexport const HelpPage = clientEntry(\\n  import.meta.url,\\n  function HelpPage(handle) {\\n    createRegisterWebMCPTools(handle, webMCPTools, {\\n      onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\\n    })\\n\\n    return () =>\\n      createElement(\\n        'section',\\n        { id: 'help-panel', popover: 'auto' },\\n        createElement('h2', {}, 'Help'),\\n      )\\n  },\\n)\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changes to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" value replace registrations in React, Preact, and Octane. Stable values prevent unnecessary registry changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All wrappers accept "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":". A contextual client tool makes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" and the options argument required."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"migrate-from-the-earlier-wrapper-names","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrate from the earlier wrapper names"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The earlier names still work, but they are deprecated. They will be removed in 1.0.0:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current name"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useWebMCPTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRegisterWebMCPTools"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createWebMCPTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRegisterWebMCPTools"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectWebMCPTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectRegisterWebMCPTools"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The options types have the same change, for example "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseWebMCPToolsOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" becomes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"use-the-framework-neutral-registrar","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the framework-neutral registrar"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If another lifecycle owns the registration, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"registerWebMCPTools"},{"type":"text","value":". The required signal controls how long the tools stay registered."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { registerWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst registration = new AbortController()\n\nawait registerWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n  signal: registration.signal,\n  toolOptions: {\n    open_help_panel: {\n      title: 'Open help',\n      annotations: {\n        readOnlyHint: false,\n        untrustedContentHint: false,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport function disposeWebMCPTools() {\n  registration.abort()\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disposeWebMCPTools()"},{"type":"text","value":" from the explicit teardown path for your application shell. Do not use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pagehide"},{"type":"text","value":", because BFCache can restore the page."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The annotations are hints for the browser agent. They do not enforce permissions or approval."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"understand-the-execution-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understand the execution boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebMCP calls the client handler directly. The result returns directly to WebMCP and does not continue a TanStack chat run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The execution context has these WebMCP rules:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" is the WebMCP execution signal. Pass it to cancellable browser APIs."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" is the value from the registrar or wrapper options."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" does nothing because no TanStack stream exists."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":" is absent because WebMCP does not provide one."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The registration signal and the execution signal have different jobs. The registration signal removes tools, while the execution signal cancels one call."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancellation is cooperative. Your handler must observe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" or pass it to an API that supports cancellation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validate-data-at-the-page-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate data at the page boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The registrar converts each input schema to JSON Schema for WebMCP discovery."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a Standard Schema, it validates input before execution. It also validates output before the result returns to WebMCP."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A raw JSON Schema only describes the data. TanStack AI does not use it for runtime validation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you use raw JSON Schema, validate untrusted input inside the handler. Return a value that matches the output schema."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool results must be JSON-serializable. WebMCP reports a serialization failure to its caller."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-the-security-boundary-on-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the security boundary on the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsApproval: true"},{"type":"text","value":" tools cannot register with WebMCP. WebMCP annotations cannot enforce the TanStack approval contract."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not expose a sensitive action only through a browser check. The server endpoint must enforce authentication, authorization, rate limits, and business rules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool names must be unique. Duplicate names in one call fail before registration changes the document registry."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebMCP also rejects a name that another owner already registered. If registration fails, the registrar removes only the tools added by that call."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If WebMCP is available, your page now exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"open_help_panel"},{"type":"text","value":". Other browsers continue to use the page without that agent action."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-install-the-packages","text":"1. Install the packages","level":2},{"id":"2-define-an-executable-client-tool","text":"2. Define an executable client tool","level":2},{"id":"3-register-the-tool","text":"3. Register the tool","level":2},{"id":"migrate-from-the-earlier-wrapper-names","text":"Migrate from the earlier wrapper names","level":3},{"id":"use-the-framework-neutral-registrar","text":"Use the framework-neutral registrar","level":2},{"id":"understand-the-execution-boundary","text":"Understand the execution boundary","level":2},{"id":"validate-data-at-the-page-boundary","text":"Validate data at the page boundary","level":2},{"id":"keep-the-security-boundary-on-the-server","text":"Keep the security boundary on the server","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","octane","remix","vanilla"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have a browser action that a page agent needs to discover and execute. WebMCP exposes your TanStack client tools through `document.modelContext`.\n\n> **Experimental:** WebMCP support is experimental. Use it as progressive enhancement, not as a required application path.\n\nDuring SSR, in insecure contexts, or in unsupported browsers, registration resolves without adding tools. Your application continues to work without WebMCP.\n\nThis page sends your tools to WebMCP. To give the WebMCP tools on a page to your own chat, see [Page WebMCP Tools in Chat](./webmcp-page-tools).\n\n## 1. Install the packages\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react zod\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-vue zod\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-solid zod\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-svelte zod\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-preact zod\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-angular zod\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client zod\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-octane octane zod\nremix: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-remix remix zod\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## 2. Define an executable client tool\n\nDefine the tool at module scope. A browser agent executes the tool to open a help panel.\n\n```ts\n// tools.ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const openHelpPanel = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'open_help_panel',\n  description: 'Open the help panel for a topic',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    topic: z.string(),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    opened: z.boolean(),\n  }),\n}).client((input) => {\n  const panel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#help-panel')\n  if (!panel) {\n    return { opened: false }\n  }\n\n  panel.dataset.topic = input.topic\n  panel.showPopover()\n  return { opened: true }\n})\n\nexport const webMCPTools = [openHelpPanel]\n```\n\nWebMCP requires an executable `.client()` implementation. It also requires a nonempty description and a valid tool name.\n\nA tool name can contain 1 to 128 ASCII letters, numbers, underscores, hyphens, or periods.\n\n## 3. Register the tool\n\nUse the lifecycle wrapper for your framework. Each wrapper removes its registrations during owner cleanup.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a component. If its contents do not change, keep the tool array stable.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst webMCPOptions = {\n  onError(error: unknown) {\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\n  },\n}\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Vue\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a setup scope. Vue removes the registrations during scope disposal.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nuseRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n  onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <section id=\"help-panel\" popover>\n    <h2>Help</h2>\n  </section>\n</template>\n```\n\n# Solid\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a reactive owner. Solid removes the registrations during owner cleanup.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\nCall `createRegisterWebMCPTools` in the component script. Svelte removes the registrations during component destruction.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n  import { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\n  createRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n  })\n</script>\n\n<section id=\"help-panel\" popover>\n  <h2>Help</h2>\n</section>\n```\n\n# Preact\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a component. If its contents do not change, keep the tool array stable.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst webMCPOptions = {\n  onError(error: unknown) {\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\n  },\n}\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Angular\n\nCall `injectRegisterWebMCPTools` in an injection context. Angular removes the registrations through `DestroyRef`.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-angular'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-help-page',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: '<section id=\"help-panel\" popover><h2>Help</h2></section>',\n})\nexport class HelpPage {\n  webMCP = injectRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n  })\n}\n```\n\n# Octane\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a component. If its contents do not change, keep the tool array stable.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-octane'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst webMCPOptions = {\n  onError(error: unknown) {\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\n  },\n}\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Remix\n\nPass the component `Handle` to `createRegisterWebMCPTools`. Remix uses `handle.signal` for cleanup.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\nimport { clientEntry, createElement } from 'remix/ui'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nexport const HelpPage = clientEntry(\n  import.meta.url,\n  function HelpPage(handle) {\n    createRegisterWebMCPTools(handle, webMCPTools, {\n      onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n    })\n\n    return () =>\n      createElement(\n        'section',\n        { id: 'help-panel', popover: 'auto' },\n        createElement('h2', {}, 'Help'),\n      )\n  },\n)\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nChanges to the `tools` or `options` value replace registrations in React, Preact, and Octane. Stable values prevent unnecessary registry changes.\n\nAll wrappers accept `toolOptions`, `context`, and `onError`. A contextual client tool makes `context` and the options argument required.\n\n### Migrate from the earlier wrapper names\n\nThe earlier names still work, but they are deprecated. They will be removed in 1.0.0:\n\n| Deprecated name     | Current name                |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `useWebMCPTools`    | `useRegisterWebMCPTools`    |\n| `createWebMCPTools` | `createRegisterWebMCPTools` |\n| `injectWebMCPTools` | `injectRegisterWebMCPTools` |\n\nThe options types have the same change, for example `UseWebMCPToolsOptions` becomes `UseRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions`.\n\n## Use the framework-neutral registrar\n\nIf another lifecycle owns the registration, use `registerWebMCPTools`. The required signal controls how long the tools stay registered.\n\n```ts\nimport { registerWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst registration = new AbortController()\n\nawait registerWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n  signal: registration.signal,\n  toolOptions: {\n    open_help_panel: {\n      title: 'Open help',\n      annotations: {\n        readOnlyHint: false,\n        untrustedContentHint: false,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport function disposeWebMCPTools() {\n  registration.abort()\n}\n```\n\nCall `disposeWebMCPTools()` from the explicit teardown path for your application shell. Do not use `pagehide`, because BFCache can restore the page.\n\nThe annotations are hints for the browser agent. They do not enforce permissions or approval.\n\n## Understand the execution boundary\n\nWebMCP calls the client handler directly. The result returns directly to WebMCP and does not continue a TanStack chat run.\n\nThe execution context has these WebMCP rules:\n\n- `abortSignal` is the WebMCP execution signal. Pass it to cancellable browser APIs.\n- `context` is the value from the registrar or wrapper options.\n- `emitCustomEvent` does nothing because no TanStack stream exists.\n- `toolCallId` is absent because WebMCP does not provide one.\n\nThe registration signal and the execution signal have different jobs. The registration signal removes tools, while the execution signal cancels one call.\n\nCancellation is cooperative. Your handler must observe `abortSignal` or pass it to an API that supports cancellation.\n\n## Validate data at the page boundary\n\nThe registrar converts each input schema to JSON Schema for WebMCP discovery.\n\nFor a Standard Schema, it validates input before execution. It also validates output before the result returns to WebMCP.\n\nA raw JSON Schema only describes the data. TanStack AI does not use it for runtime validation.\n\nIf you use raw JSON Schema, validate untrusted input inside the handler. Return a value that matches the output schema.\n\nTool results must be JSON-serializable. WebMCP reports a serialization failure to its caller.\n\n## Keep the security boundary on the server\n\n`needsApproval: true` tools cannot register with WebMCP. WebMCP annotations cannot enforce the TanStack approval contract.\n\nDo not expose a sensitive action only through a browser check. The server endpoint must enforce authentication, authorization, rate limits, and business rules.\n\nTool names must be unique. Duplicate names in one call fail before registration changes the document registry.\n\nWebMCP also rejects a name that another owner already registered. If registration fails, the registrar removes only the tools added by that call.\n\nIf WebMCP is available, your page now exposes `open_help_panel`. Other browsers continue to use the page without that agent action.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: WebMCP Tools\nid: webmcp\norder: 5\ndescription: \"Expose TanStack AI client tools to browser agents through the experimental WebMCP API.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - webmcp\n  - browser agents\n  - client tools\n  - registerWebMCPTools\n  - useRegisterWebMCPTools\n  - createRegisterWebMCPTools\n  - injectRegisterWebMCPTools\n---\n\nYou have a browser action that a page agent needs to discover and execute. WebMCP exposes your TanStack client tools through `document.modelContext`.\n\n> **Experimental:** WebMCP support is experimental. Use it as progressive enhancement, not as a required application path.\n\nDuring SSR, in insecure contexts, or in unsupported browsers, registration resolves without adding tools. Your application continues to work without WebMCP.\n\nThis page sends your tools to WebMCP. To give the WebMCP tools on a page to your own chat, see [Page WebMCP Tools in Chat](./webmcp-page-tools).\n\n## 1. Install the packages\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react zod\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-vue zod\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-solid zod\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-svelte zod\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-preact zod\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-angular zod\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client zod\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-octane octane zod\nremix: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-remix remix zod\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## 2. Define an executable client tool\n\nDefine the tool at module scope. A browser agent executes the tool to open a help panel.\n\n```ts\n// tools.ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const openHelpPanel = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'open_help_panel',\n  description: 'Open the help panel for a topic',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    topic: z.string(),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    opened: z.boolean(),\n  }),\n}).client((input) => {\n  const panel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#help-panel')\n  if (!panel) {\n    return { opened: false }\n  }\n\n  panel.dataset.topic = input.topic\n  panel.showPopover()\n  return { opened: true }\n})\n\nexport const webMCPTools = [openHelpPanel]\n```\n\nWebMCP requires an executable `.client()` implementation. It also requires a nonempty description and a valid tool name.\n\nA tool name can contain 1 to 128 ASCII letters, numbers, underscores, hyphens, or periods.\n\n## 3. Register the tool\n\nUse the lifecycle wrapper for your framework. Each wrapper removes its registrations during owner cleanup.\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a component. If its contents do not change, keep the tool array stable.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst webMCPOptions = {\n  onError(error: unknown) {\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\n  },\n}\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Vue\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a setup scope. Vue removes the registrations during scope disposal.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nuseRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n  onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <section id=\"help-panel\" popover>\n    <h2>Help</h2>\n  </section>\n</template>\n```\n\n# Solid\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a reactive owner. Solid removes the registrations during owner cleanup.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-solid'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Svelte\n\nCall `createRegisterWebMCPTools` in the component script. Svelte removes the registrations during component destruction.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { createRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n  import { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\n  createRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n  })\n</script>\n\n<section id=\"help-panel\" popover>\n  <h2>Help</h2>\n</section>\n```\n\n# Preact\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a component. If its contents do not change, keep the tool array stable.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-preact'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst webMCPOptions = {\n  onError(error: unknown) {\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\n  },\n}\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Angular\n\nCall `injectRegisterWebMCPTools` in an injection context. Angular removes the registrations through `DestroyRef`.\n\n```ts ignore\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-angular'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-help-page',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: '<section id=\"help-panel\" popover><h2>Help</h2></section>',\n})\nexport class HelpPage {\n  webMCP = injectRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n    onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n  })\n}\n```\n\n# Octane\n\nCall `useRegisterWebMCPTools` in a component. If its contents do not change, keep the tool array stable.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-octane'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst webMCPOptions = {\n  onError(error: unknown) {\n    console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error)\n  },\n}\n\nexport function HelpPage() {\n  useRegisterWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, webMCPOptions)\n\n  return (\n    <section id=\"help-panel\" popover=\"auto\">\n      <h2>Help</h2>\n    </section>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Remix\n\nPass the component `Handle` to `createRegisterWebMCPTools`. Remix uses `handle.signal` for cleanup.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createRegisterWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\nimport { clientEntry, createElement } from 'remix/ui'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nexport const HelpPage = clientEntry(\n  import.meta.url,\n  function HelpPage(handle) {\n    createRegisterWebMCPTools(handle, webMCPTools, {\n      onError: (error) => console.error('WebMCP registration failed', error),\n    })\n\n    return () =>\n      createElement(\n        'section',\n        { id: 'help-panel', popover: 'auto' },\n        createElement('h2', {}, 'Help'),\n      )\n  },\n)\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nChanges to the `tools` or `options` value replace registrations in React, Preact, and Octane. Stable values prevent unnecessary registry changes.\n\nAll wrappers accept `toolOptions`, `context`, and `onError`. A contextual client tool makes `context` and the options argument required.\n\n### Migrate from the earlier wrapper names\n\nThe earlier names still work, but they are deprecated. They will be removed in 1.0.0:\n\n| Deprecated name     | Current name                |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `useWebMCPTools`    | `useRegisterWebMCPTools`    |\n| `createWebMCPTools` | `createRegisterWebMCPTools` |\n| `injectWebMCPTools` | `injectRegisterWebMCPTools` |\n\nThe options types have the same change, for example `UseWebMCPToolsOptions` becomes `UseRegisterWebMCPToolsOptions`.\n\n## Use the framework-neutral registrar\n\nIf another lifecycle owns the registration, use `registerWebMCPTools`. The required signal controls how long the tools stay registered.\n\n```ts\nimport { registerWebMCPTools } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { webMCPTools } from './tools'\n\nconst registration = new AbortController()\n\nawait registerWebMCPTools(webMCPTools, {\n  signal: registration.signal,\n  toolOptions: {\n    open_help_panel: {\n      title: 'Open help',\n      annotations: {\n        readOnlyHint: false,\n        untrustedContentHint: false,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport function disposeWebMCPTools() {\n  registration.abort()\n}\n```\n\nCall `disposeWebMCPTools()` from the explicit teardown path for your application shell. Do not use `pagehide`, because BFCache can restore the page.\n\nThe annotations are hints for the browser agent. They do not enforce permissions or approval.\n\n## Understand the execution boundary\n\nWebMCP calls the client handler directly. The result returns directly to WebMCP and does not continue a TanStack chat run.\n\nThe execution context has these WebMCP rules:\n\n- `abortSignal` is the WebMCP execution signal. Pass it to cancellable browser APIs.\n- `context` is the value from the registrar or wrapper options.\n- `emitCustomEvent` does nothing because no TanStack stream exists.\n- `toolCallId` is absent because WebMCP does not provide one.\n\nThe registration signal and the execution signal have different jobs. The registration signal removes tools, while the execution signal cancels one call.\n\nCancellation is cooperative. Your handler must observe `abortSignal` or pass it to an API that supports cancellation.\n\n## Validate data at the page boundary\n\nThe registrar converts each input schema to JSON Schema for WebMCP discovery.\n\nFor a Standard Schema, it validates input before execution. It also validates output before the result returns to WebMCP.\n\nA raw JSON Schema only describes the data. TanStack AI does not use it for runtime validation.\n\nIf you use raw JSON Schema, validate untrusted input inside the handler. Return a value that matches the output schema.\n\nTool results must be JSON-serializable. WebMCP reports a serialization failure to its caller.\n\n## Keep the security boundary on the server\n\n`needsApproval: true` tools cannot register with WebMCP. WebMCP annotations cannot enforce the TanStack approval contract.\n\nDo not expose a sensitive action only through a browser check. The server endpoint must enforce authentication, authorization, rate limits, and business rules.\n\nTool names must be unique. Duplicate names in one call fail before registration changes the document registry.\n\nWebMCP also rejects a name that another owner already registered. If registration fails, the registrar removes only the tools added by that call.\n\nIf WebMCP is available, your page now exposes `open_help_panel`. Other browsers continue to use the page without that agent action.\n"}
